# /etc/default/sloth-sdrsweep — site configuration for
# sloth-sdrsweep.service (docs/wiki/sdr-sweep.md).
#
# Read by systemd as an EnvironmentFile: KEY=value, one per line, no
# shell expansion and no quoting (a value may contain spaces). `make
# install-service` installs this file only when there is none, so an
# edited copy is never replaced. Every line is optional; the values
# below are the helper's own defaults, for an SDRplay RSPdx-R2.
#
# Nothing a browser sends reaches these: slothweb's "Run" button only
# creates a request file, and the helper reads this file and its unit's
# command line, never the request.
#
# The SoapySDR device string. Add serial=... when more than one is
# attached (`SoapySDRUtil --find`); the string form, not key/value
# pairs, is what opens an SDRplay through SoapySDRPlay3.
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_DEVICE=driver=sdrplay
#
# The receive port the antenna is on. slothweb shows this name, so a
# reader of the waterfall knows why bands far from the antenna's design
# look empty.
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_ANTENNA=Antenna A
#
# Fixed gain, gain mode off: SoapySDRPlay3's element names, in dB of
# reduction (more IFGR is less gain).
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_GAIN=IFGR=40,RFGR=3
#
# The span, in MHz, clamped to the device's tuning range.
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_F_LO_MHZ=0.5
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_F_HI_MHZ=2000
#
# Seconds of whole sweeps (each one a row of the waterfall), and the
# least time, in seconds, between the end of one run and the next.
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_DURATION=60
#SLOTH_SDRSWEEP_COOLDOWN=600
